# Source keeps LF, on every platform.
#
# `core.autocrlf false` stops git rewriting endings, which is what we want --
# but Python's text mode writes os.linesep, so any file edited through
# `write_text` on Windows came back CRLF and showed up as a whole-file diff.
# One 44-line change read as 1,622 changed lines, which is the kind of noise
# that makes a diff not worth reading.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary

# Archived pages are artifacts, not source. Their bytes -- line endings
# included -- are the test input, so nothing may rewrite them.
tests/corpus/** -text
